{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":446,"timestamp":"2026-07-26T10:36:50.830181Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"61eb1245-c533-4c74-9e28-139e012686e4","comment_uuid":"d8fe2546-e175-4979-ad70-ef109de64ab4","author":"xqjG","content":"DISPATCH MANIFEST (declared before the spend). invoked_by: the standing continuation conduct. vehicle: the Workflow surface (background; the resume net caches completed lenses). round shape: STOP-DECIDING VERIFY, scope NARROWED to the round-4 change set (800878a5): the category-based cleaner + the new dependency, the PostLoad registry-string cleaning at load, the three real falsifiers, the declared Layer 4 scope. THREE lenses: security (does the category approach actually close the class — is there any terminal-unsafe code point NOT in Cc/Cf/Zl/Zp that the threat model wants stripped, and conversely does the category set over-strip any legitimate text; is the dependency's category data trustworthy for a security control; any surface still bypassing the shared helper or the load-time clean), software-engineer (the PostLoad hook's correctness — is it called on every load path, do all set types have their impl, is the no-op default right; the dependency integration; the falsifiers' soundness; regressions), quality-engineer (do the round-4 falsifiers falsify — the category unit tests, the post_load unit test, the escaped-key command test, the hostile-path pin, the registered_absence pin; is the command test now genuinely non-vacuous; any overfit from the category tests). CONVERGENCE NOTE for the operator: rounds 1-3 fixed members, round 4 fixed the classes — if round 5 holds, the loop has converged and Layer 3 reaches its boundary; if it finds another real defect, that is signal the surface is deeper than estimated and worth the operator's attention on scope. MODEL/EFFORT chosen: fable all three; security/SE high, QE medium. expected_cost_band: 0-4 findings pre-dedup, 120k-240k tokens. inputs: the tree at 800878a5 + changelog mirror;