{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":480,"timestamp":"2026-07-27T17:34:59.949105Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ffcf310c-2090-45c8-9fbe-b63080f8b305","comment_uuid":"e242a067-d85f-4b0d-b941-d244c7e9b405","author":"xqjG","content":"ROUND 6 RETURNED — 2 of 3 lenses (the quality lens died mid-response on a connection drop, the 4th interruption of this layer's dispatches; a dead lens is not a clean verdict, so it needs a cached re-run, but the security lens already refuses the stop). Verdicts: #798/#800/#801 held; #799 incomplete. Stop: NOT reached. Children: #803 (major security: active_composition.config_inputs_hash — the FOURTH ActiveComposition string field — is uncleaned at read_state and serialized raw into the machine form; #799 cleaned scope, domains, and phase and missed this sibling; demonstrated on the built binary with U+202E/U+200B/U+2060/tag/U+E0000 all reaching machine-form stdout), #804 (minor security+SE convergent: assigned default-ignorable Hangul fillers U+115F/1160/3164/FFA0, category Lo, are invisible in common terminal fonts but pass the Cc/Cf/Zl/Zp+unassigned filter — the only default-ignorable survivors outside a declared preservation decision), #805 (nit collector: comparison-only state fields uncleaned, intra-state asymmetry, broken human machine_token raw). TELEMETRY: 235,560 tokens across the 2 completed lenses; chosen=observed fable, security/SE high. CONVERGENCE ASSESSMENT, honest: this is the THIRD 'N-1 of N' occurrence — chars (enumerated, missed members), registry strings (cleaned 2, found 4 more), now composition fields (cleaned 3, missed 1). The member-by-member fixing does not converge because I keep hand-picking which fields to clean. There IS a systematic fix that converges by construction (recursively sanitize the machine-form JSON output, catching every field regardless of struct shape), but that is an architectural choice. Per the round-6 manifest's pre-commitment — another real major means pause and reassess scope with the operator, not continue — I am NOT dispatching round 7. Surfacing the decision to the operator with the systematic option as the recommendation. #803's one-line field fix is trivial; the question is whether to do the systematic fix that ends the class or make a scope call.","created_at":"2026-07-27T17:34:59.935391Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAl5whtvPEA8Dlrg+ZqwMoFV61lDlZWC/Hw1symvIz3WTfFOpYKyCv0gLoZBsypHHT7zMyslgjGNGII9NfENTjDA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKBqj7vcEHMWd0SUKylXoeJV42MQmyuKjCyhgGBZ1GmHktNpLoG3y3gA+Z/6dYVgiRcEdQDPqxtrYB1MZ8aILAk="}
