{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":491,"timestamp":"2026-07-27T18:14:56.910632Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9483fa7a-0f91-4485-8f60-abef77a51e26","comment_uuid":"735364f7-2e89-4b56-9a03-2c52852a1df5","author":"xqjG","content":"PHASE-4 ROUTING (under the #806 format-carry). Routing question — what artifact, had it been correct, would have prevented config_inputs_hash reaching the machine form raw? Not the implementation: the DESIGN.md Status requirement never specifies terminal-output safety at all, so there was no spec to build the sanitization against and no boundary saying which fields it covers. ROUTE TO: Phase 1a/1b — the terminal-safety spec amendment (drafted next on this trail). config_inputs_hash is one member of the terminal-safety class; it is covered for free by the amendment's systematic sink (recursive machine-form sanitization) and its mechanism (the Default_Ignorable UCD property), not by another hand-picked field patch. NOT fix-closed in Layer 3; stays open, routed, until the amendment lands and the rebuild verifies.","created_at":"2026-07-27T18:14:56.895470Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAt1WE1nO4sZzEuMr1COvPEqPPa+CIXJiHf20EvxiLMKUo2NBPI2NdkzL/JftGYw6GI883QN6Dx0yqLNB+YhSIDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF0QZK0myQ9zlUJYZRe8On8xnymU/idsQXi3hWfBjfmR9/14enLfQP7AvlnwtSHOeco6GRcLi/1FM4uPG9GdHAI="}
{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":492,"timestamp":"2026-07-27T18:15:03.315153Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"06fcba1d-8071-46a0-a588-b1a0579c0db2","comment_uuid":"aa4416cd-e3cc-4132-9f31-e80d9c1a3712","author":"xqjG","content":"PHASE-4 ROUTING (under the #806 format-carry). The Hangul fillers are the same class as #803/#798 — assigned default-ignorable code points. Correct-artifact answer: the spec requirement + the right mechanism. ROUTE TO: Phase 1a/1b terminal-safety amendment; the Default_Ignorable_Code_Point UCD property covers them by construction (the amendment retires the hand-rolled category+range+enumeration classifier that has been finding 'one more code point' every round). NOT fix-closed; routed, open until the amendment's rebuild.","created_at":"2026-07-27T18:15:03.300905Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAtzKRLmfqUuPVBp7yYXD94sHA+N60kTnDNXhnKnadGH+/+0htvurXccBpTUQnDAycxs5SpSjJ6fEJ1MQacNLrBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQORPoCA0s4ycocOvY3RIR+NWN9WA2gfGiHKV1cqLmbtmoPpJjG+XgVKjhW7XDnr1C0uRLmR7vQdiov/Vu71C5QQ="}
