{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":494,"timestamp":"2026-07-27T18:15:38.697568Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ffcf310c-2090-45c8-9fbe-b63080f8b305","comment_uuid":"fd147b57-38ca-47ee-8fce-93c0d2c6fe50","author":"xqjG","content":"ROUND 6 DISPOSITION + PHASE-3 LOOP SUSPENDED (under the #806 ratification). Round 6's findings are ROUTED, not fixed-in-place: #803/#804/#805 all route to the Phase 1a/1b terminal-safety spec amendment (routing plans recorded on each). The phase-3 loop for Layer 3 is SUSPENDED here — it was not converging by member-fixing because it was patching an UNSPECIFIED requirement (six rounds, spec unchanged, code churned: the collapse #806 names). It does not resume as more phase-3 rounds; it resumes as: (a) the terminal-safety spec amendment specifies the requirement, mechanism (Default_Ignorable UCD property), boundary (vsdd-local now + shared-primitive raise to crosslink), and systematic sink (recursive machine-form sanitization); (b) a minimal rebuild under the spec — keep the recursive JSON sanitizer, DISCARD the uncommitted round-6 Hangul enumeration (the UCD property retires it), swap the predicate; (c) ONE verify round against the now-specified requirement; (d) Layer 3 close. The falsifiability findings from earlier rounds that were fix-closed stand; the round-6 uncommitted edits are held pending the amendment. RETROSPECTIVE NOTE: rounds 1-5's terminal-safety fixes are real and landed (they close genuine injection vulnerabilities) but were built without a governing spec — the amendment supplies the spec they should have had, and their tests become its verification architecture. This is the routing that should have happened at round 1.","created_at":"2026-07-27T18:15:38.684625Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA