{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":502,"timestamp":"2026-07-27T18:31:58.599905Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"627c8f6a-1181-4ae6-8dac-157a63c17dd7","comment_uuid":"315086f8-e316-45af-b69e-e137015e9644","author":"xqjG","content":"THE DEVIATION (recorded; the record stands per the ungated-work discipline).\n\nWHAT: contract amendments #806 (routing format-carry + invariant-first principle) and #807 (terminal-output-safety requirement + shared-primitive boundary raise) were authored and committed directly to the ratified governing document (.design/agent-first-vsdd-toolkit.md) by a single agent inside a Layer-3 EXECUTION session, on operator content-approval alone.\n\nWHY IT IS A DEVIATION — two ways, one root:\n1. VSDD process: a spec amendment is a re-entry into phase 1a/1b — authored under a declared composition, run through cold review lenses, THEN ratified. Operator approval is the phase EXIT (the ratification gate), never a substitute for the phase's composition and review. The amendment was inlined into execution with neither; the earlier amendments (#730, #739) were legitimate precisely because they ran under the phase-1c spec-review loop with rounds and dispositions.\n2. Domain ownership (operator guidance): spec-contract changes are the Solution Owner's to author; the prose and register are Documentation Reviewer / Technical Writer's. A solo agent editing the contract's normative text and register bypassed all three owning domains.\n\nROOT: this is the same collapse the whole session has been catching — an owned, reviewed process skipped in favor of solo-act-on-approval. #806 was findings orphaned by skipping phase 4; this is an amendment orphaned by skipping phase 1a/1b. Third occurrence of the pattern this session.\n\nREMEDIATION (operator-directed, path A): reverted in commit 9b451099 (contract restored to 25851ca0; mdatron clean). The drafted text is preserved on #806/#807 and re-enters phase 1a/1b as the DRAFT — no drafting lost, but it now gets the composition and cold review it skipped, with operator ratification as the true exit. #806 and #807 reopened for that re-entry. The deviation record stands regardless of the redo.","created_at":"2026-07-27T18:31:58.584808Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAXJmGp/4R71L5SyguYo2UhGoYnGAheA0xkjWiw4VbPF5/vv6+YjNemIf+TEefQ2xfvWe9l3ZB99ky8n7y4Zk4Dw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH9JZXNfuiXUjy9Sh6IcZGVoZYsakGA4Fu0yGT8cUNv4fH9UWMNu9KG8Ed3iH1VYE7V23f3jIzAJpk1nnSqOpwc="}
