{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":552,"timestamp":"2026-07-28T03:04:46.332990Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5972e95a-9098-40c1-9b8e-320d7df410a3","comment_uuid":"57e893cc-5f71-4f10-8609-2da711b14a83","author":"xqjG","content":"PHASE-1A/1B RE-ENTRY — STANDALONE COMPOSITION DECLARATION (declared before spend). The 19:58 declaration bundled #806+#807 as one review under [SO, SA, DR, TW]; execution split them — #810 carried the #806 material (ratified, #811 built), and the re-sequence draft's Out-of-Scope explicitly carved terminal-safety out to its own track. This is that track. Standalone scope CORRECTS the composition: a Trojan-Source / display-spoofing amendment with a dependency swap requires a SECURITY lens (absent from the bundled decl) — running it without one would be a composition defect.\n\nreview draft: .design/terminal-output-safety.md (clause text from the #807 18:17 draft, re-entered under review)\n\ncomposed_domains: [solution-owner (primary), security (co-primary), solution-architect, documentation-reviewer, technical-writer]\ncomposition_mode: attended-design (cold lenses under the session permission flow; operator present)\ndelta_from_confirmed: +security (co-primary); dependency-surface question (unicode-properties vs the tree's unicode-general-category) folded into the SA + security remits rather than a separate PE lens, to hold the lens count at five.\n\nOwning-domain rationale: SO holds spec-contract change authority (the requirement, the trust-boundary member); Security owns the threat model (class completeness, the source+whole-output sink, the Trojan-Source framing, the security-critical dependency); SA reviews architecture (clause placement, the shared-primitive boundary, the purity split, layer scope); DR cold-reads clarity + implicit-knowledge gaps; TW guards register, plain-naming, and the Revision-line entry.\n\nDISPATCH MANIFEST. vehicle: Workflow, attended side. round shape: SPEC-AMENDMENT REVIEW over the drafted clause text (not code). MODEL: claude-fable-5 all five. EFFORT: SO / security / SA HIGH (substantive spec, threat, and architecture judgment), DR / TW MEDIUM. expected_cost_band: 0-15 findings pre-dedup, 150k-320k tokens. output: per-lens findings (wrong / missing / mis-scoped / unclear / mis-registered) + each lens verdict (sound-as-drafted vs revise-before-ratify). After: route findings, revise the draft, terminal + final verify, bring revised draft to operator for ratification as the phase EXIT. Layer-3 rebuild stays parked until then.","created_at":"2026-07-28T03:04:46.318987Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAk0ldYEqAdI3pTdblgQT0ZPekSgjdLKCJ6AA76U1jkz7rAVPHXJbTQ4Nv715SFZE8YSu2Lb+RmNN3xyLV+actAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGmZXbrvdkhEZ5m8Z4qUV5/abBlm3rAPUry6eF5cCmWH1Zf7vwcZdUHuY4oxJLKvlFinWLhApqwDoJucONXTCQ0="}
{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":553,"timestamp":"2026-07-28T03:15:10.387287Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5972e95a-9098-40c1-9b8e-320d7df410a3","comment_uuid":"a1bcce0a-ae9e-4db4-8097-641a9422eec8","author":"xqjG","content":"COLD REVIEW RETURNED — 5/5 lenses revise-before-ratify (fable-5, 276k tokens, within the 150-320k band; 0 dispatch failures). 43 findings, deduped to 24 distinct. TRIAGE + ROUTING (routing before fixing):\n\nCONVERGENT BLOCKERS (multiple independent lenses):\n- D1 [Security+SA, both BLOCKING]: the strip-set and preserve-set OVERLAP. Default_Ignorable_Code_Point includes variation selectors (U+FE00-FE0F, U+E0100-E01EF), the combining grapheme joiner, Mongolian VS — all category Mn. REQ-2 says strip all Default_Ignorable AND preserve Mn/Mc/Me: contradiction, no precedence. AND the draft's 'no behavioral loss' claim is FALSE — text.rs's variation_selectors_survive test pins U+E0100 as KEPT (#798 ruling), which a pure property predicate strips. -> OPERATOR TRIAGE (reverses #798; security-vs-fidelity).\n- D2 [SO BLOCKING]: scope. REQ-1's 'agent-consumed surface' generality is silently narrowed to Status's 4 forms, leaving generated agent context (built from the adopter registry — the biggest agent-context pipeline, the named threat's prime target) and gate outputs neither bound nor excluded. -> OPERATOR TRIAGE.\n- D3 [SO+Security+SA+DR, 4 lenses]: the dual sink is not gapless. Broken-state human diagnostic composes from a FAILED read (upstream of every source boundary, not the machine form so no whole-output backstop) and can quote raw adopter bytes; shell-joined git-ref strings and the statusline repo-set config load also escape the 3 named boundaries. -> FIX PASS.\n\nOPERATOR-TRIAGE (spec-intent / structure):\n- D4 [SO->Trust-boundaries(c); SA->standalone requirement(b); both reject Status-clause(a)]: clause placement. -> OPERATOR TRIAGE.\n- D9 [Security]: confusables/homoglyphs (CVE-2021-42694, the OTHER Trojan Source CVE) neither in nor out of scope; no stripping class catches them. -> OPERATOR TRIAGE (propose: out-of-scope accepted residual).\n\nFIX-PASS (self-resolvable, folding into the revised draft):\n- D5 [SO+SA]: #739 three-question procedure MISCITED — it governs mdatron check-needs and literally forbids the raise; record as a plain crosslink-tracker proposal, #739 as precedent only.\n- D6 [SO+SA+DR]: REQ-6 carries transient content (round-6 uncommitted-edit disposition, clean_json_strings identifier, 'uncommitted') into standing contract text — keep durable mechanism, move edit-disposition to the decision record.\n- D7 [SO+Security+DR]: REQ-1 external-source parenthetical reads exhaustive but omits repo-set config, artifact manifest, settings, .vsdd/config.yaml — define as complement-of-trusted-constants, anchor to Trust-boundaries enumeration, mark illustrative.\n- D8 [Security]: CRATE — neither unicode-general-category nor unicode-properties carries the property; Default_Ignorable_Code_Point is a DerivedCoreProperties binary property, not General_Category. icu_properties (ICU4X) is the verified-capable candidate; forbid hand-deriving from category data (that IS the rejected enumeration).\n- D10 [SA]: the whole-of-output pass is unclassified vs the purity enumeration; classify as a pure filter applied once by the shell at output (not a second derivation).\n- D11 [Security]: machine-form backstop exempts JSON keys on an unstated invariant; clean keys too (identity on the trusted case) or state the invariant with a falsifier.\n- D12 [TW]: draft has NO verbatim clause text — only REQ-level descriptions; add a 'Proposed contract text' section with the exact insertions + Revision entry so the words shipping are the words reviewed (cures the #808-shaped gap).\n- D13 [TW+SO+DR]: AC-8 Revision anchor wrong — anchor on the re-entry issue carrying ratification (not #807), name composition + terminal-verify round, put #807/#808 in motivated-by.\n- D14/D15 [Security]: name accepted residuals —