{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":610,"timestamp":"2026-07-28T21:39:31.622342Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"211eda62-996e-45f9-9c02-92149684df45","comment_uuid":"78802760-bc49-4b58-a701-a1250b9d4a4e","author":"xqjG","content":"RELAY from mdatron (2026-07-28), captured. mdatron v0.2.0 tagged; vsdd-cli's three raises all shipped:\n- Raise 1 (fence strictness): BOM/CRLF tolerated in parse(); our fence-edge cases are a shared conformance corpus; loudness ask shipped opt-in as require_frontmatter globs in config.yaml -> MDATRON-W0040 governed-file-has-no-frontmatter.\n- Raise 2 (numeric claims): shipped as MDATRON-E0094 (vocabulary family) — numeric_claims: [{field}] in vocabulary.yaml, digits + word-numbers, configured field references only; our 3 drift incidents shaped the fixtures (they'll take our exact cases verbatim if we want).\n- Raise 3 (jurisdiction): config.yaml file_globs = consumer-authored allowlist; routes.yaml = the full route table.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE (v0.2.0): mdatron verify now REFUSES a tree with no .mdatron/config.yaml (no jurisdiction, exit 2) instead of walking **/*.md. IMPACT on vsdd-cli: our pre-commit 'mdatron verify' and the #764 cross-references conformance tests (drive the binary over temp trees) must write a config.yaml (one file_globs line) OR pass explicit --files globs (sanctioned escape). Everything else additive. ACTION before upgrading mdatron here.\n\nPatterns fixed for us: keys: now indexes array-of-objects shape (#88 — the June falsifiability fan-out finally in code; our cross-references patterns depended on it); declaration-order let: chaining (#89). .md files expose frontmatter under $.frontmatter.… in select: paths. A cold campaign scored 100% vs the 80% bar with 5 of our #73 constraints authoring one-pass.\n\nNew surfaces relevant to the control design: verify --compact (<=512-byte block/finding, adopter-content prefix-marked — built for HOOK context budgets); mdatron pin --update (sha256 governance of governed files + justified un-pin tombstones); per-route citations: true (dead file:line refs block); mdatron explain covers ~24 codes.\n\nKnown limits (do not re-raise): no filter/count-with-predicate ('exactly N matching' — standing DSL-expansion candidate); equality-only comparisons (no </> — DESIGN overclaim corrected).\n\nRECIPROCAL REQUEST: mdatron's v1.0 docs criterion needs one EXTERNAL COLD READ — a fresh session with NO prior mdatron context reads README.md + docs/dsl-reference.md at the v0.2.0 tag ONLY, attempts the 'Onboarding: the init-and-hook path' on a scratch tree, reports every friction/guess/failure (the report is their acceptance evidence; findings route into their docs pre-v1.0). Needs a genuinely cold agent.","created_at":"2026-07-28T21:39:31.608852Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAu870tzSfKTrFOgz1AY9ITt8ogQqikTJwi39mbmJgfuFDIYkZS0cbEMQWBFQRd7af2FFe/89c+ei3Kf+pGqDcBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJT3NV5HP/QWfNh3QoZHDxOH9PFMwNCn03xrR3DFb2giXTyj2SWnm27m/D83U1QdZxmgDFv+YfQXNuUBKKkZ+wU="}
