{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":620,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T00:33:45.304964Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"211eda62-996e-45f9-9c02-92149684df45","comment_uuid":"b5361b1a-e3ca-4707-af59-5aeec6cc636b","author":"xqjG","content":"mdatron #49 COLD READ complete (fresh agent, read only v0.2.0 README + dsl-reference, attempted init-and-hook on a scratch tree). VERDICT: partially — the HOOK half works flawlessly from the README alone (pre-commit wiring, clean/diagnostic verify, explain, --json, --project-root all match); the INIT half is blocked.\n\nBlockers/friction, by cause:\nVERSION-GAP (local binary is mdatron 0.1.0, docs are v0.2.0 — clears if installed from a v0.2.x checkout per README l.30-31 'cargo install --path mdatron --locked'): 'mdatron init' absent (the one non-optional onboarding step); 'mdatron pin' absent (onboarding step 4); 'verify --compact' absent; the no-config error says 'run mdatron init first' (which doesn't exist) instead of the documented 'no jurisdiction declared' — a circular dead-end.\nDOC-INTRINSIC (would remain even on v0.2.0): (3) config.yaml format is never shown in either doc — no example, no field list — so 'scope your jurisdiction' is unfollowable; (4) output-marking discipline violated — the adopter field name rides INLINE in the engine note ('= note: Additional properties are not allowed (\\'extra\\' was unexpected) ()', raw jsonschema string + trailing '()'), no prefix-marked '= unexpected:' quoted block as README l.83-86 promises; (8) namespace contradiction — README pattern example uses code MDATRON-W0100 while dsl-reference l.28-29 says MDATRON-* is reserved for the engine; (5 nit) source span is absolute-path, line-only, column 0 vs the documented rustc-shape 'bad.md:3:1'.\n\nFINDING THAT MATTERS FOR OUR INTEGRATION: we are on 0.1.0; every v0.2.0 capability the agent-first-controls design leans on (pin --update, verify --compact, config.yaml jurisdiction) is ABSENT until we install v0.2.0 (cargo install --path ../mdatron --locked). Reinforces the config.yaml migration + #764 harness work folded into #815. Full report available for relay to mdatron (routes into their docs pre-v1.0).","created_at":"2026-07-29T00:33:45.287280Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAy7XNkpUhpnlXjN7v6iKuCpeyzcjEoZX4ELH8e7NY1MBnKPrp98C7vtXorpuPt8T5TWOI0tG26vv6jpRQdq0xBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMOn/xwhUCWtWxUIyhuPssl/T7DZ7Uf7sQJy10hgBpm633We1okFmImlBdD7nbYNQHDJnXrrO6OO1ekotrOCvQ0="}
{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":621,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T00:37:11.909308Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"211eda62-996e-45f9-9c02-92149684df45","comment_uuid":"b9f7802e-2d09-48eb-8a88-9645731201d7","author":"xqjG","content":"CONSOLIDATED FEEDBACK to mdatron (v0.3.0 prioritization CROSS-INFORMED by the #49 cold-read — the cold-read produced live evidence that updates our ranking, so this supersedes the two prior comments as the coherent relay):\n\nWHAT THE COLD-READ CHANGES IN OUR PRIORITIZATION:\n- B (contract-stability + audit hardening) — STILL FIRST, now with LIVE EVIDENCE, not just design-preference. The cold-read caught the shipped binary VIOLATING the documented output-marking discipline: the adopter field name rides INLINE in the engine note ('= note: Additional properties are not allowed (\\'extra\\' was unexpected) ()' — raw jsonschema string + trailing '()'), with no prefix-marked '= unexpected:' block (README l.83-86 promises one). That is exactly what B's envelope schema + the 'verify --compact adopter-content-prefix-marked' surface exist to fix. And it matters doubly for us: our agent-first-controls design reads mdatron output as a TRACE (the conformance leg of the mechanism-invocation-timing audit); adopter content bleeding into engine lines is a trace-integrity problem — we can't cleanly separate engine signal from adopter text. So: B first, and the output-envelope/marking hardening is the specific sub-item, evidenced.\n- config.yaml documentation is a PREREQUISITE, not a nit. The cold-read could not scope jurisdiction because config.yaml's format is shown NOWHERE in README or dsl-reference. This blocks (a) any cold adopter and (b) OUR #764 migration — the v0.2.0 breaking change requires us to author a config.yaml, and we can't author to an undocumented format. Please document config.yaml (fields + an example) as part of / ahead of the jurisdiction (A) and B work.\n- Install-from-v0.2.x prominence (docs + UX). The cold-read ran the stale 0.1.0 on PATH and the entire init-half broke silently (init/pin/--compact absent; no-config error said 'run mdatron init first' — which doesn't exist — instead of the documented 'no jurisdiction declared'). Onboarding should fail-loud on a version/binary mismatch, or make the 'cargo install --path mdatron --locked' step unmissable.\n\nUNCHANGED: A second (rising with our action-time hooks; ~178 files / 0.65s pre-commit on 0.1.0). D1 (filter/count-with-predicate) third. C/D2 lower. E: yes to the numeric-claims fixture intake.\n\n#49 docs findings (route to their docs): config.yaml format undocumented; output-marking inline violation; namespace contradiction (README example uses MDATRON-W0100 which dsl-reference reserves for the engine); no-config error wording mismatch; source-span is absolute-path/line-only/column-0 vs documented rustc shape; version-gap prominence. What worked README-only: the whole pre-commit hook path, clean/diagnostic verify, explain, --json, --project-root.\n\nOUR STATUS: on 0.1.0; will install v0.2.0 (cargo install --path ../mdatron --locked) as part of #764 migration folded into #815.","created_at":"2026-07-29T00:37:11.875993Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA7ZANOshcI8Ex/xNmXaPST9bllKqvURt+sRp8Uy19bvkn09s5GA4yEjoGGPKycuOP4Y4FE8/49PW6LsGhuxPhBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPfRv4JqrVUs/QrqIVDcJryeG9IfpenyRNs6s90hYAZMITqfYZOC0psaeb0pUxU3U+YEgkgy+0FwtcnTqRtZWQw="}
{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":622,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T00:37:20.506067Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6b24050a-4513-4856-895f-71388315fa63","comment_uuid":"b953a50e-8e11-4be0-9179-b2c52b319d9f","author":"xqjG","content":"DESIGN DEPENDENCY from the #49 cold-read (fold into the post-cold-review revision): the mdatron-vehicle controls (the conformance leg of the mechanism-invocation-timing audit) read mdatron output as a TRACE. The cold-read found v0.1.0 bleeds adopter content INTO engine lines (inline field names, raw jsonschema strings) — a trace-integrity hazard for us. So the design's mdatron-conformance leg DEPENDS on mdatron's output-envelope/marking discipline (v0.3.0 cluster B) being solid; record that dependency + prefer the machine envelope (--json / the published envelope schema) over parsing human-form engine lines. Not editing the doc now (under cold review); apply in the revision.","created_at":"2026-07-29T00:37:20.485903Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA01PARTXZg0rFLHlmdFpqFDJNKR4cvERQVN/g9JjkSJF0pyxq3ZRiS37Zgk5cb6jXX0yCtwatK1v48gUVhzqyCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD8lrD+8IFuE3TthGEfkhJNNM4ZQDslthuX15/nEEUtxbBm3NB/0dacCCnRdIeETmL3cW6BmbWGgJNsP1J+pLwo="}
{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":623,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T00:40:44.819984Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6b24050a-4513-4856-895f-71388315fa63","comment_uuid":"16f4f885-65e4-466f-ae84-29cf1d97babe","author":"xqjG","content":"COLD REVIEW (Opus 4.8, 7 lenses) — UNANIMOUS 7/7 revise-before-ratify; ~15 blocking/substantive deduped. TRIAGE (route before fixing):\n\nFIX-PASS (I resolve in the revision):\n- Trace substrate: RE-BASE off the retired .vsdd/events/ store onto the contract's derived-view model (state.yaml active-composition field, boundary commit history, milestone closes, typed result comments — a query, not a store) [SA blocking]; ADD a trace-integrity requirement (git history + tracker integrity, not agent-editable logs) so traces aren't forgeable/self-authored [Security blocking].\n- Keystone home: make it ONE thing — a single-home Status aggregate control that CONSUMES mdatron conformance records as inputs (the #810 Layer-2-query-consumed-by-Layer-6-gate pattern), not a frame+control+double-homed surface [SA+SO blocking].\n- VSDD-E0050: REMOVE the 'contracted' assertion (it's nowhere in the contract) — describe the condition plainly (phase-composition-not-declared) OR mark it a proposed allocation through the owning phase; the coinage reflex again [SO+Security+QE+DR/TW — 4 lenses].\n- REQ-3 routing: reconcile with the ratified mechanism — the routing IS the  comment (contract l.77 + #810 carry); the dependency edge is an ADDITION, not a replacement; don't re-mechanize what #810 format-carried [SO blocking + SA].\n- Cost: add a requirement+AC for a per-session hook wall-clock budget + per-control firing cadence + cost-banding/model-tier (not prose only) [AIE blocking + substantive].\n- Revision-line entry: DRAFT it (AC-9 requires it; absent) [SO+DR/TW].\n- Fixtures: specify the 3 regression fixtures concretely + fix the middle-bypass named 3 ways [QE+DR/TW].\n- Also: self-governance layer owner (not 'throughout'); non-vacuity defined; pin --update = shape-tier, don't assign it truth-tier amendment authorization (tier-rule); the dependency-free tripwire emitting external content must route through the #807 cleaner; keystone gets a real falsification AC; L1/L2 phase-5 deferral gets a retest trigger; re-sequencing delta over #810 stated; note contract text uses plain leading names not REQ-n.\n\nOPERATOR DECISIONS (two prior resolutions rested on premises the review overturned):\n(A) Dogfood 'first blocking control now' — the review shows it needs the Layer-4/7 hook seam, NOT dependency-free-now. Buildable-now form is non-blocking DETECTION.\n(B) mdatron fold-in — no migration path, crosses the repo boundary, breaks live CI; sequence separately (#816) may be cleaner.\n\nNext: operator re-decides (A)+(B); I run the fix pass on the rest; terminal verify; ratification.","created_at":"2026-07-29T00:40:44.804792Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA/wGs8PWfLAzco1pMAlK/0uGBA9ViuOTrB8ANqVqoPvvORxX82fJ3oWrzhOkHs1932llaA7mNW/ZV3k/ReAF+Cg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIvEv5Y2Yyq0jh1NdGn3QRt6Q0bQ7RNr4Fg7vcwqIgJtyAMcMPOgbPWNEAKq17d/7QgudGc4fXXobNAEqyO2gAA="}
