{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":654,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T02:58:49.988138Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6b24050a-4513-4856-895f-71388315fa63","comment_uuid":"4f575518-34ee-484d-ad0e-f6e47e07638f","author":"xqjG","content":"Thermite architecture study (agent report 2026-07-28); filed dollspace-gay/Thermite#93 for its enforcement drift. Lessons for #815 (the tamper-proof / grade-4 half):\n1. Tool-allowlist-per-role IS real grade-4 — Claude Code refuses an ungranted tool (verified: acto-critic lacks Edit). BUT a capability fence is only as strong as the FULL residual set: Thermite's critic still holds Write+Bash, so its 'read-only' is grade-1 convention, not capability. A genuine read-only critic must withhold EVERY mutation tool (drop Write, constrain Bash) or run on a read-only mount. This is precisely WHY #815's tamper-evidence-by-corroboration half stays necessary — it covers the residual Write/Bash surface a porous fence cannot.\n2. Add a LIVENESS axis orthogonal to the 4 grades: a designed grade is worthless if de-wired. Thermite's two edit-time gates silently died (commit 5581b65f) and every doc still claims them live. The meta-harness must ROUTE ITS OWN CONTROL PLANE (settings.json, agent defs) — a gate that guards the gates. Directly reinforces the vsdd draft's own 'route the control plane' instinct.\n3. Split grade 2: 2a commit/push-time (records a deviation) vs 2b edit-time PreToolUse (prevents the edit) — 2b is closer to grade-4 in effect and still substrate-portable; a sweet spot for controls that can't be grade-4.\n4. Match doc claims to enforced reality mechanically. Thermite's goal.md R-SIDE-1/R-BV-1 'forward-looking — not yet enforced' labels are the good model; make 'enforced' a checked property (a test asserting the claimed wiring exists).","created_at":"2026-07-29T02:58:49.926573Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjD