{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":663,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:23:07.138869Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"440db558-bd72-4bc6-8c3e-c188cc37b16e","comment_uuid":"0596ddd8-202e-41c7-9dc5-bdfe8038b9e0","author":"xqjG","content":"UN-STUCK (operator direction 2026-07-28). Rescheduled from 'the mdatron session's cycle / when the collapse schedules' to land WITH the engine/Slice-1 work (phase-2a). No longer a perpetual punt.\n\nSCOPE CORRECTION: the FULL single-crate collapse in this issue's title is SUPERSEDED for vsdd -- the cost crate (Slice 7) requires a workspace, so vsdd stays a 2-crate workspace. The actual pending act is narrower: REMOVE the vsdd-core crate by merging it into the vsdd binary crate, leaving {vsdd, cost} (the #739 2026-07-22 marker: 'both cores planned for removal').\n\nWHY HERE: the engine (ratified #819) IS the re-characterized vsdd-core -- state/snapshot/derivation/queries -- plus the binary's renderings; and Slice 1 already rewrites acquire.rs inside vsdd-core (the tracker-join). Merging the crate boundary away while that code is being touched is the natural moment; the slice's crate-level module map is a phase-2a act per #819, so the merge is decided/executed there.\n\nVSDD SUB-QUESTION DECIDED: the cost crate keeps the vsdd workspace (yes -- it is why full collapse is superseded). The other #739 sub-question (whether mdatron's single crate keeps a lib target) is mdatron's, excluded here.\n\nCONTRACT TOUCH: the Architecture-section workspace-shape paragraph ('this paragraph takes its amendment when the collapse schedules') now takes that scoped amendment -- ROUTED to an owned cycle (bundle with the terminology follow-on, or the Slice-1 phase-1a/1b entry), never solo-hand-edited. Issue title is now inaccurate for vsdd (full-collapse wording); retitle to 'vsdd-core removal (merge into the vsdd binary crate; cost workspace retained)' when convenient.","created_at":"2026-07-29T04:23:07.121795Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:v2