{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":673,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T05:02:31.081575Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ccced380-4c00-4475-bd76-75a386e41968","comment_uuid":"2dfc715f-d0c1-4afe-bfba-a10571fe5142","author":"xqjG","content":"PHASE-2A DESIGN ACTS (grounded in the live crosslink surface, verified 2026-07-28):\n1. Finding discrimination (bootstrap rule): a finding is an issue whose PARENT is a review-round issue (parent carries label 'review'). Verified: #750 parent_id=745, #745='Phase 3 execution... adversarial refinement round 1' label ['review']. This is the bootstrap format-carry; Slice 5's filing convention formalizes it.\n2. SCOPE REFINEMENT: Slice 1's tracker-join reads only the ENFORCEMENT-SPINE fields the unrouted-findings query needs -- discrimination, routing_present (a 'plan'-kind comment; verified kind exists), closed_before_ratification (closed_at vs the ratification boundary), status/disposition. owner/validator/evidence_reference_present are NOT crosslink-native (verified: finding #750 has no such fields, only a 'result' comment) -- they depend on Slice 5's filing convention, so reading them at Slice 1 would back-depend on a later slice (DAG violation). They stay bootstrap-empty until Slice 5. Recorded as a Slice-1 scope decision.\n3. Test seam: pure mappers (routing_present, is_finding-via-parent-review-label, closed_before_ratification-vs-boundary) unit-tested with canned crosslink JSON; a few real-crosslink integration tests over a temp repo. Red gate = failing-executed on the positive/after assertions against minimal mapper bodies.","created_at":"2026-07-29T05:02:31.049453Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAEtChYz4DO1nM2tMO+JpG+ziRqZunvD+mxbWkhhbsvRnW0ATJsDWmOPy1tpb7d10U2DzGy9PcPS4wFdhWX63IBA=="},"signed_by":"S