{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":675,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T05:22:09.867229Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ccced380-4c00-4475-bd76-75a386e41968","comment_uuid":"93ae89c6-ee0c-41e5-93f3-d7c3dcc0c6e6","author":"xqjG","content":"PHASE-2A/2B STATUS — honest boundary reached (design decision required before the effectful read).\nVERIFIED THIS SESSION: (1) discrimination rule is crisp — a finding = an issue whose PARENT is 'review'-labeled (finding #750 parent=745[review] subissues=0; rounds have parent=None+subissues; work issues no parent). is_finding(parent_labels) is the correct design. (2) Red gate increment 1 (3 mapper tests: routing_present/is_finding/closed_before_ratification) verified RED — failing-executed, non-vacuous. REVERTED from the working tree (git checkout acquire.rs) to avoid an orphaned dead-code red gate; re-lands WITH the effectful read in the focused 2b, trivially reproducible from this record.\nTHE 2B DESIGN DECISION (the real blocker, surfaced by grounding — the AIE cost finding, live): reading findings-with-routing needs a 'crosslink issue show' PER finding ('issue list --json' omits comments/labels) = O(n) subprocess calls. acquire_snapshot runs on the statusline (250ms budget), so O(n) findings there is a budget hazard. Two forks to resolve before coding: (a) TWO-PATH acquisition — lightweight statusline acquire (findings feed integrity/health-detail via a PULL, not the hot segment) vs a fuller acquire for the guardrail/CI path; (b) within the full path: bulk query vs bounded per-finding shows vs cache. CHEAPEST FIX + raise candidate: an UPSTREAM crosslink bulk findings+comments export (issue export --json interface returned nothing parseable; confirm or raise). Flag to Platform Engineer — benefits every crosslink adopter.\nQUEUED behind the effectful-read design: the assembler (assemble_findings), acquire wiring, guardrail verdict wrapper (wraps snapshot_integrity's unrouted-findings), the commit-msg hook + CI leg, and the vsdd