{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":682,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T06:42:17.994287Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"211eda62-996e-45f9-9c02-92149684df45","comment_uuid":"b6792f36-c663-456e-a97c-f24b468d2456","author":"xqjG","content":"MDATRON 0.1.0 -> 0.3.0 UPGRADE FEEDBACK (from vsdd-cli's actual flip, 2026-07-28 — adoption experience; the clear-to-publish #48 verdict still follows after a couple slices per operator):\n\nWORKED WELL:\n1. E0080 jurisdiction path: migration was config.yaml ALONE, no code/corpus changes. 'no jurisdiction declared' pointed straight at the fix.\n2. `mdatron init` idempotency + the adopter/managed split is the standout. On a mirror of our exact hand-built 0.1.x layout, init added ONLY the missing managed manifest.yaml and preserved our adopter-owned config.yaml verbatim (hash-checked). The adopter-owned (config.yaml) vs managed (manifest.yaml, 'do not edit by hand', E0060) partition is clean and the seeded files state their own ownership. Refusing a hand-modified managed file with E0060 is exactly right.\n3. families report (#90): emitted on verify --json. Good.\n4. Tag hygiene: v0.3.0 properly bumps Cargo.toml to 0.3.0.\n5. End-to-end: our pre-commit guardrail ran v0.3.0 verify live during the flip commit — clean.\n\nFEEDBACK / QUESTIONS FROM REAL USE:\nA. families active/inactive SEMANTICS need documenting — this is load-bearing for us. On a CLEAN run (0 findings) we get schema=active, vocabulary/route/pin/citation=inactive, EVEN THOUGH we set vocabulary_globs (methodology.md, DESIGN-*.md). So 'active' is not 'produced findings' (run was clean) and 'inactive' is not 'not configured' (vocabulary IS configured). For families to serve as the un-invoked-mechanism audit signal we asked for, we need to distinguish 'invoked, ran, nothing to act on (clean)' from 'not invoked / not applicable'. Please document precisely what active vs inactive mean, ideally tri-state.\nB. init discoverability on 0.1.x->0.3.x upgrades: we hand-built .mdatron/ under 0.1.x and never knew to run init; verify is clean WITHOUT manifest.yaml, so nothing surfaced the missing managed manifest. E0080 flagged config.yaml but nothing pointed at the manifest gap. Suggest a migration note ('run mdatron init after upgrading') or a verify hint when .mdatron/ predates the managed-manifest layout.\nC. pin (#84): `mdatron pin` reports 'no pin record (pins.yaml absent)'. Is pins.yaml part of the recommended adoption baseline, or an advanced opt-in? init does not scaffold it. Clarify in adoption docs.","created_at":"2026-07-29T06:42:17.965585Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAr/nyqAP7grO1KSqL1eFk5A+9oQuMYW2wUxyIFuo1kNOHJKL9kEPtdqhQ7E3L2i4+WCTyF3I41EFTOlOLcOecAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA13qs52FSwzsd/ulaGzerl1BzHAev+zzuiCrhrl1FV9/821ID3HyqdryJAzXTL2uZn4UPiuqtM3pBjTbIsPNAE="}
