{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":685,"timestamp":"2026-07-29T07:12:36.405194Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"211eda62-996e-45f9-9c02-92149684df45","comment_uuid":"2080b230-e980-440e-8899-322391f32e51","author":"xqjG","content":"FLIP FALLOUT (discovered dogfooding v0.3.0) — the v0.3.0 flip BROKE vsdd's own cross-reference conformance tests (cross_references.rs E0207 + E0208). Correcting the record: 'mdatron verify clean on the real corpus' held, but the TEST SUITE went red at the flip commit (3ea9cdb7). ROOT CAUSE: cross_references.rs builds a temp mdatron project and runs the mdatron BINARY over it; the E0207/E0208 rules live alongside a key('domains',...) rule in cross-references.yaml whose index source is templates/registry/composition-scope-and-actions.md. mdatron v0.3.0 HARD-FAILS the whole pipeline (MDATRON-E0080, 'index build error: file IO ... No such file or directory', files_checked=0) when that key-index source is absent, taking down the unrelated E0207/E0208 rules with it. 0.1.0 tolerated the missing index. The TempProject harness seeds schemas+patterns+fixture but NOT the index source (nor a config.yaml). FIX DIRECTION (open): (a) update the harness to seed config.yaml + the domains-index source so the temp project is complete under v0.3.0; AND/OR (b) mdatron feedback — is whole-pipeline-fail on a missing key-index source intended, vs failing only the dependent rule? This is substantive v0.3.0-behavior feedback feeding #48. ALSO: iCloud made a byte-identical conflict-copy 'convergence_red_gate 2.rs' of an actively-edited file (repo lives under ~/Documents) — removed; the repo under an iCloud-synced dir is a hazard.","created_at":"2026-07-29T07:12:36.367433Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAU+a3GznuYuLrPKSS4GcnLYKJwCKrdMov